<title>GERMANY: West German consumer prices remain subdued in Sept.</title>
<headline>West German consumer prices remain subdued in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>West German consumer prices remained subdued in September, falling 0.1 percent from the previous month to post annual inflation at a preliminary 1.4 percent, the Federal Statistics Office said.</p>
<p>Both figures were identical with the final August data, the office said. The office will publish final, nationwide data for September in mid-October.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
